1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,750
Arjun can’t tell his family what he wants without feeling
ungrateful.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,800
Private reflection you can correct before exploring peer
experiences.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,800
Muse Spark may organize possibilities for review, not decide.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,520
This is a prepared local example; no model is connected.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,800
A prepared local reply offers one possibility, not a
decision.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,950
He chooses Not quite.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:34,105
He changes partner to parents, and asks for time.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:38,105
The changed reflection keeps his wording.

9
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:44,195
This reply came from prepared local rules, not Muse Spark.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,400
Arjun’s correction changes the reflection.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,205
He chooses whether to explore lived experience.

12
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,140
Fictional historical posts show a different perspective.

13
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:04,615
Ravi also wanted time; it did not settle Arjun’s question.

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:09,590
Day nine: the host says, I can listen; I can’t decide for
you.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,145
The example shows a prepared hold; no report is sent.

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,235
Day sixteen: Dev’s side question still has no replies.

17
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:24,775
These are prepared fictional posts, not live community
activity.

18
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,870
Arjun edits his question to Ravi.

19
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,110
The exact preview changes with his words.

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:39,120
It names the group and alias; replies stay group-only.

21
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:43,145
His private conversation is excluded.

22
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:48,635
Consent is unchecked; sending is disabled.

23
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,700
Nothing is sent from this preview.

24
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,110
No provider is verified or bookable here.

25
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,325
He returns to the peer thread, then keeps a takeaway
privately.

26
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,790
He wants time to decide; that thought stays private.

27
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,005
Maybe later leaves sharing optional.

28
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:17,295
He chooses one bounded thing he could offer Dev.

29
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:22,160
He types a local draft in his own words.

30
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,130
He can review its exact text and group audience.

31
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,785
The private context is excluded.

32
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,625
Consent stays unchecked; the post action stays disabled.

33
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,890
The draft remains local and unsent.

34
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,065
Arjun’s next step stays his choice.

35
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,715
Nothing is sent without consent.

36
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,020
He can leave it here.
